1
00:00:25,792 --> 00:00:28,125
♪♪

2
00:00:36,370 --> 00:00:38,305
♪♪

3
00:00:49,349 --> 00:00:51,341
♪♪

4
00:01:53,347 --> 00:01:55,339
♪♪

5
00:02:23,310 --> 00:02:25,302
♪♪

6
00:02:34,688 --> 00:02:35,898
<i>Hi, I'm Patrick,</i>

7
00:02:35,922 --> 00:02:37,834
and I'm a compulsive gambler.

8
00:02:37,858 --> 00:02:39,135
Hi, Patrick.

9
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:41,037
Here we are again...
The Wednesday night

10
00:02:41,061 --> 00:02:43,106
participation meeting
of the West Side group

11
00:02:43,130 --> 00:02:44,540
of Gamblers Anonymous.

12
00:02:44,564 --> 00:02:45,842
Okay.

13
00:02:45,866 --> 00:02:47,977
And, newcomers, welcome.

14
00:02:48,001 --> 00:02:50,046
You're in the right place.

15
00:02:50,070 --> 00:02:53,040
Ty, come on up and let's
start off this clambake.

16
00:02:57,077 --> 00:03:00,056
Patrick.

17
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:02,892
My name is Ty, and I'm
a compulsive gambler.

18
00:03:02,916 --> 00:03:05,328
Hi, Ty.

19
00:03:05,352 --> 00:03:08,231
Some of you who attended
last Friday's meeting

20
00:03:08,255 --> 00:03:09,699
heard me going on about

21
00:03:09,723 --> 00:03:13,670
my 138 consecutive
days not gambling

22
00:03:13,694 --> 00:03:18,474
and about how important
the program is to me

23
00:03:18,498 --> 00:03:21,044
and how great it
is to feel free again;

24
00:03:21,068 --> 00:03:25,048
how great it is to like myself.

25
00:03:25,072 --> 00:03:27,405
I bet you thought,
"He's on a roll."

26
00:03:29,643 --> 00:03:32,221
I bet you thought, he's
gotten the program.

27
00:03:32,245 --> 00:03:36,225
I bet you looked up here
at me blowing my own horn

28
00:03:36,249 --> 00:03:38,548
and said, "He's a winner."

29
00:03:40,253 --> 00:03:43,246
If that's your bet, you lose.

30
00:03:45,325 --> 00:03:48,318
'Cause that's
what I am: a loser.

31
00:03:50,464 --> 00:03:54,510
The very next day, the guy who
owns the club I'm working in...

32
00:03:54,534 --> 00:03:57,480
He started talking to me
about the Atlanta Falcon game,

33
00:03:57,504 --> 00:04:00,406
the point spread and how
the quarterback was hurt.

34
00:04:02,409 --> 00:04:04,954
And I started
thinking... Bad move.

35
00:04:06,012 --> 00:04:07,810
You got that right.

36
00:04:09,816 --> 00:04:12,462
Well, we all know
the end of the story.

37
00:04:12,486 --> 00:04:14,797
I made a bet.

38
00:04:14,821 --> 00:04:15,798
One bet.

39
00:04:15,822 --> 00:04:20,603
That bet cost me my 138 days.

40
00:04:20,627 --> 00:04:23,239
And $25,000.

41
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:25,775
I don't have $25,000.

42
00:04:25,799 --> 00:04:28,678
You know, they say

43
00:04:28,702 --> 00:04:32,682
you have to suffer
to sing the blues.

44
00:04:32,706 --> 00:04:34,150
Hell, I'm singing
better than ever.

45
00:04:35,175 --> 00:04:36,652
♪ I was raised up ♪

46
00:04:36,676 --> 00:04:38,654
♪ On Jimmy Reed ♪

47
00:04:40,313 --> 00:04:45,595
♪ Corn bread, collard
greens and black-eyed peas ♪

48
00:04:45,619 --> 00:04:51,033
♪ Took my first bath
in muddy water ♪

49
00:04:51,057 --> 00:04:52,368
♪ All you mamas ♪

50
00:04:52,392 --> 00:04:55,671
♪ Better watch your daughters ♪

51
00:04:55,695 --> 00:04:59,029
♪ I'm a blues man... ♪

52
00:05:00,233 --> 00:05:01,277
This guy is great!

53
00:05:01,301 --> 00:05:02,278
Didn't I tell you?

54
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:04,464
♪ I'm a blues man ♪

55
00:05:07,541 --> 00:05:10,204
♪ I'm a blues man ♪

56
00:05:12,212 --> 00:05:16,206
♪ I'm a blues man ♪

57
00:05:18,218 --> 00:05:20,463
♪ I'm an original ♪

58
00:05:20,487 --> 00:05:23,232
♪ One of a kind ♪

59
00:05:23,256 --> 00:05:25,902
♪ I don't do nothing ♪

60
00:05:25,926 --> 00:05:27,360
♪ What's on my mind... ♪

61
00:05:28,361 --> 00:05:29,572
All right.

62
00:05:29,596 --> 00:05:31,440
Listen, I'll be sure
to send you a copy.

63
00:05:31,464 --> 00:05:34,577
Thanks again.

64
00:05:34,601 --> 00:05:36,312
Hey, guys, you made it.

65
00:05:36,336 --> 00:05:37,980
Sherry, come here.

66
00:05:38,004 --> 00:05:39,615
I want you to take
a picture of me

67
00:05:39,639 --> 00:05:42,351
with my three oldest
buddies in the entire world.

68
00:05:42,375 --> 00:05:44,053
Four gorgeous hunks.

69
00:05:44,077 --> 00:05:45,121
Squeeze in, come on.

70
00:05:45,145 --> 00:05:47,137
Come on, guys,
smile for the lady.

71
00:05:50,150 --> 00:05:51,194
Come on.

72
00:05:51,218 --> 00:05:53,429
My private table.

73
00:05:53,453 --> 00:05:55,631
Thanks, babe.

74
00:05:55,655 --> 00:05:58,989
♪ I'm a blues man ♪

75
00:06:00,794 --> 00:06:04,207
♪ I'm a B... ♪

76
00:06:04,231 --> 00:06:07,443
♪ L... U... ♪

77
00:06:07,467 --> 00:06:08,444
All right.

78
00:06:08,468 --> 00:06:10,313
You are a gin and tonic,

79
00:06:10,337 --> 00:06:14,684
beer and a...
bourbon, straight up.

80
00:06:14,708 --> 00:06:17,653
Just cut the crap and tell us
what the hell this is all about.

81
00:06:17,677 --> 00:06:21,657
Well, fellas, I just seem to
be a little strapped for cash.

82
00:06:21,681 --> 00:06:23,172
Wondering if you
could help me out.

83
00:06:24,751 --> 00:06:26,529
We can't handle
any more of this.

84
00:06:26,553 --> 00:06:28,798
This is the last time, boys.

85
00:06:28,822 --> 00:06:30,333
Uh-huh.

86
00:06:30,357 --> 00:06:31,500
Last time.

87
00:06:42,736 --> 00:06:43,746
All right.

88
00:06:43,770 --> 00:06:44,747
Break it down, man.

89
00:06:44,771 --> 00:06:46,649
I'll check you in a minute.

90
00:06:46,673 --> 00:06:48,184
Hey, Ty, that was great.

91
00:06:48,208 --> 00:06:49,619
Thank you, man.

92
00:06:49,643 --> 00:06:50,820
Hey, hey, Ty.

93
00:06:50,844 --> 00:06:51,888
Ben! How's it going?

94
00:06:51,912 --> 00:06:53,122
All right!

95
00:06:53,146 --> 00:06:54,790
My friend here didn't
believe I know you.

96
00:06:54,814 --> 00:06:56,125
Ty Mullins,

97
00:06:56,149 --> 00:06:57,360
- this is Conrad McMasters.
- Conrad.

98
00:06:57,384 --> 00:06:58,361
You were great.

99
00:06:58,385 --> 00:06:59,595
- Didn't I tell you?
- Yeah.

100
00:06:59,619 --> 00:07:01,430
Yeah. How long
you gonna be here?

101
00:07:01,454 --> 00:07:02,832
Well, actually, it looks like

102
00:07:02,856 --> 00:07:04,533
this might be my
home for a while.

103
00:07:04,557 --> 00:07:05,534
All right.

104
00:07:05,558 --> 00:07:06,636
You'll see a lot of us.

105
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:07,637
Want a drink?

106
00:07:07,661 --> 00:07:08,938
Sure.

107
00:07:08,962 --> 00:07:10,873
You know, I have some
business to take care of.

108
00:07:10,897 --> 00:07:12,041
Can I take a rain check?

109
00:07:12,065 --> 00:07:14,577
- You got it.
- Right. Hey, Conrad.

110
00:07:14,601 --> 00:07:16,279
- Nice to meet you, Ty.
- Nice to meet you.

111
00:07:16,303 --> 00:07:18,114
Ben, it's always great.

112
00:07:18,138 --> 00:07:19,115
- Yeah.
- See you later.

113
00:07:19,139 --> 00:07:20,249
- Great, huh?
- Yeah.

114
00:07:20,273 --> 00:07:21,350
Didn't I tell you?

115
00:07:21,374 --> 00:07:22,385
Yeah.

116
00:07:22,409 --> 00:07:25,121
Come on, fellas, relax.

117
00:07:25,145 --> 00:07:27,690
It's not like you have
a whole lot of choice.

118
00:07:27,714 --> 00:07:28,714
Eric.

119
00:07:30,383 --> 00:07:32,395
- Eric, I need to talk to you.
- Later.

120
00:07:32,419 --> 00:07:34,697
Look, man, you owe the
guys more than a grand!

121
00:07:34,721 --> 00:07:36,198
I know.

122
00:07:36,222 --> 00:07:37,733
And you owe me 25 grand, see,

123
00:07:37,757 --> 00:07:39,268
so don't you start
leaning on me.

124
00:07:39,292 --> 00:07:40,536
Look, I'm not asking for myself.

125
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:42,204
- I'm asking for the band.
- Back off!

126
00:07:42,228 --> 00:07:44,322
Not until you pay 'em.

127
00:07:48,501 --> 00:07:52,381
Look, let's, uh, let's
just calm down, huh?

128
00:07:52,405 --> 00:07:55,034
We'll settle this tomorrow,
my office, 10:00 a.m.

129
00:07:56,743 --> 00:07:58,735
Cash money.

130
00:08:07,988 --> 00:08:10,833
Sorry about that.

131
00:08:10,857 --> 00:08:12,335
So what do you say, fellas?

132
00:08:12,359 --> 00:08:14,704
$50,000 apiece ought to do it.

133
00:08:14,728 --> 00:08:16,772
Damn bloodsucker.

134
00:08:16,796 --> 00:08:19,508
This is the last
time, you got that?

135
00:08:19,532 --> 00:08:20,543
This is it.

136
00:08:20,567 --> 00:08:22,445
That's what I said.

137
00:08:22,469 --> 00:08:23,612
Come on, fellas.

138
00:08:23,636 --> 00:08:26,649
I don't hit you up
on a regular basis.

139
00:08:26,673 --> 00:08:28,403
Just when I need it.

140
00:09:15,155 --> 00:09:17,147
♪♪

141
00:09:29,269 --> 00:09:31,580
Did you bring the money?

142
00:10:03,069 --> 00:10:05,181
Davis.

143
00:10:05,205 --> 00:10:07,183
Hey, Davis.

144
00:10:23,690 --> 00:10:25,835
Yo, Eric.

145
00:10:25,859 --> 00:10:26,859
Eric.

146
00:10:29,863 --> 00:10:31,024
Oh...

147
00:10:45,345 --> 00:10:47,123
Look, hurry.

148
00:10:47,147 --> 00:10:49,692
Send the police to
Gaston's Blues Club.

149
00:10:49,716 --> 00:10:50,793
There's a man shot here.

150
00:10:50,817 --> 00:10:51,817
Hurry!

151
00:11:12,872 --> 00:11:14,083
I don't know how

152
00:11:14,107 --> 00:11:16,051
the money or the
gun got in my car,

153
00:11:16,075 --> 00:11:17,086
I swear.

154
00:11:17,110 --> 00:11:18,154
It's not your gun?

155
00:11:18,178 --> 00:11:19,388
I hate guns.

156
00:11:19,412 --> 00:11:21,123
I've never owned one in my life.

157
00:11:21,147 --> 00:11:24,260
The police assume the money came

158
00:11:24,284 --> 00:11:26,462
from the safe in Eric's office.

159
00:11:26,486 --> 00:11:28,631
I didn't take it, Ben.

160
00:11:28,655 --> 00:11:33,536
Well, who-who knew you were
gonna be there this morning?

161
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:34,737
Nobody!

162
00:11:34,761 --> 00:11:36,639
At least I didn't tell anybody.

163
00:11:36,663 --> 00:11:38,607
Maybe Eric told Sherry but I...

164
00:11:38,631 --> 00:11:39,608
Who's Sherry?

165
00:11:39,632 --> 00:11:40,609
Sherry Brown.

166
00:11:40,633 --> 00:11:41,977
She's a hostess at the club.

167
00:11:42,001 --> 00:11:43,245
He used to date her.

168
00:11:43,269 --> 00:11:44,713
Wait a minute.

169
00:11:44,737 --> 00:11:46,048
There were three
men sitting with Eric

170
00:11:46,072 --> 00:11:47,616
when I went to talk
with him last night.

171
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:49,151
They all knew I
was gonna be there.

172
00:11:49,175 --> 00:11:50,186
Who were they?

173
00:11:50,210 --> 00:11:51,187
I don't know.

174
00:11:51,211 --> 00:11:52,588
Would this, uh, Sherry know?

175
00:11:52,612 --> 00:11:53,910
She might.

176
00:11:54,981 --> 00:11:56,745
Ty...

177
00:12:00,286 --> 00:12:02,331
I like you.

178
00:12:02,355 --> 00:12:06,735
You're certainly one of the
best singers I ever heard.

179
00:12:06,759 --> 00:12:09,672
And I want to hear
you sing some more.

180
00:12:09,696 --> 00:12:11,840
I'm gonna take you on.

181
00:12:11,864 --> 00:12:15,411
Now... what's her
name, this Sherry...?

182
00:12:15,435 --> 00:12:16,445
Brown.

183
00:12:16,469 --> 00:12:18,113
Brown, Brown...

184
00:12:18,137 --> 00:12:20,482
Maybe I better
have a talk with her.

185
00:12:20,506 --> 00:12:22,151
- Thank you, Ben.
- Yeah.

186
00:12:22,175 --> 00:12:25,287
But look... look, you
know I like to sing,

187
00:12:25,311 --> 00:12:27,289
but there's something
you don't know about me.

188
00:12:27,313 --> 00:12:28,324
What's that?

189
00:12:28,348 --> 00:12:30,426
I like to gamble.

190
00:12:30,450 --> 00:12:35,297
Well, I like to be on
the edge once in a while.

191
00:12:35,321 --> 00:12:36,332
You don't understand.

192
00:12:36,356 --> 00:12:37,633
I like to make a bet.

193
00:12:37,657 --> 00:12:40,436
Well, everybody puts a
dollar or two on the home team

194
00:12:40,460 --> 00:12:41,804
every now and then.

195
00:12:41,828 --> 00:12:44,406
Last bet I made
was for 25 grand.

196
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:48,344
You bet $25,000?

197
00:12:48,368 --> 00:12:51,213
On a football game that I lost.

198
00:12:51,237 --> 00:12:53,349
You lost $25,000?!

199
00:12:53,373 --> 00:12:55,351
Well, actually, I
owed it to my bookie

200
00:12:55,375 --> 00:12:57,970
who-who just happened
to be Eric Gaston.

201
00:12:59,045 --> 00:13:01,690
You owed $25,000

202
00:13:01,714 --> 00:13:04,927
to the man you're
charged with murdering?!

203
00:13:04,951 --> 00:13:05,495
Yeah.

204
00:13:05,519 --> 00:13:08,564
With him dead,
the debt's wiped out.

205
00:13:08,588 --> 00:13:11,033
Oh, the D.A.'s gonna
have fun with this one.

206
00:13:11,057 --> 00:13:12,735
I thought I had it licked.

207
00:13:12,759 --> 00:13:14,737
I quit going to the Gamblers
Anonymous meetings.

208
00:13:14,761 --> 00:13:16,559
I thought I was cured.

209
00:13:20,033 --> 00:13:23,445
Have you got any
other surprises for me?

210
00:13:23,469 --> 00:13:25,547
No.

211
00:13:25,571 --> 00:13:28,097
Thank God.

212
00:13:39,886 --> 00:13:40,963
Hey, Bob.

213
00:13:40,987 --> 00:13:43,198
Well, Mullins told
me he knew you.

214
00:13:43,222 --> 00:13:45,000
- Gonna represent him?
- Yeah.

215
00:13:45,024 --> 00:13:47,569
What's that?

216
00:13:47,593 --> 00:13:49,772
The victim was
wearing that ring.

217
00:13:49,796 --> 00:13:52,641
Apparently, he and the
killer had a real dustup

218
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:54,476
because Eric Gaston
arrived at the morgue

219
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:56,645
with a big cut and
bruise on his jaw.

220
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:58,881
But he gave as good as he got...

221
00:13:58,905 --> 00:14:00,182
At least one good right...

222
00:14:00,206 --> 00:14:01,750
Because that's
what's left of the ring.

223
00:14:01,774 --> 00:14:05,587
You mean he hit
the killer so hard

224
00:14:05,611 --> 00:14:07,189
he shattered the
stone in the ring?

225
00:14:07,213 --> 00:14:08,190
That's right.

226
00:14:08,214 --> 00:14:11,193
Well... there you go.

227
00:14:11,217 --> 00:14:13,562
There I go where?

228
00:14:13,586 --> 00:14:15,798
My client doesn't
have a mark on him.

229
00:14:15,822 --> 00:14:18,600
So? Maybe Gaston
didn't connect with his face.

230
00:14:18,624 --> 00:14:20,836
Maybe he hit his belt
buckle or something.

231
00:14:22,795 --> 00:14:23,972
Excuse me. Excuse me.

232
00:14:23,996 --> 00:14:25,641
Is there a Mr. Ben Matlock here?

233
00:14:25,665 --> 00:14:26,675
Yeah, I'm Ben Matlock.

234
00:14:26,699 --> 00:14:27,710
Hi, I'm Sherry Brown.

235
00:14:27,734 --> 00:14:28,777
I brought the picture.

236
00:14:28,801 --> 00:14:30,045
Oh, thank you for coming down.

237
00:14:30,069 --> 00:14:31,447
Can we talk
someplace else, please?

238
00:14:31,471 --> 00:14:33,030
Oh, sure...

239
00:14:34,273 --> 00:14:36,251
I took this when
they first came in.

240
00:14:36,275 --> 00:14:38,253
Eric asked me to.

241
00:14:38,277 --> 00:14:39,421
Oh.

242
00:14:39,445 --> 00:14:42,524
Why does this guy
look so familiar?

243
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:46,562
That's Roy Stevens.

244
00:14:46,586 --> 00:14:49,098
He's a network
sportscaster, Channel 4.

245
00:14:49,122 --> 00:14:50,966
Oh, yeah, I know him, yeah.

246
00:14:50,990 --> 00:14:52,267
You know these other guys?

247
00:14:52,291 --> 00:14:53,769
Oh, yeah.

248
00:14:53,793 --> 00:14:57,272
That's John Delaney,
he's a big agent...

249
00:14:57,296 --> 00:14:58,607
Movie stars and basketball.

250
00:14:58,631 --> 00:15:00,609
Football superstars, too.

251
00:15:00,633 --> 00:15:04,046
That's Tom Hermanski.
He breeds racehorses.

252
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:06,815
One of his horses won the
Preakness about four years ago.

253
00:15:06,839 --> 00:15:08,384
Oh.

254
00:15:08,408 --> 00:15:10,052
How did they get to
know one another?

255
00:15:10,076 --> 00:15:14,056
College... they played football
together at Baxter University.

256
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:15,524
Oh...

257
00:15:15,548 --> 00:15:17,926
Well, what did Eric want
to talk with them about?

258
00:15:17,950 --> 00:15:19,895
Oh, I... I don't know.

259
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:21,945
Uh, uh, he didn't tell me.

260
00:15:24,023 --> 00:15:27,936
You and he were, uh... close?

261
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:30,406
Very.

262
00:15:30,430 --> 00:15:32,741
Hey, Ben.

263
00:15:32,765 --> 00:15:34,910
Oh, Sherry Brown,

264
00:15:34,934 --> 00:15:37,479
this is Conrad
McMasters, investigator.

265
00:15:37,503 --> 00:15:39,281
We were just talking
about Eric Gaston.

266
00:15:39,305 --> 00:15:41,083
Did you know he was a bookie?

267
00:15:41,107 --> 00:15:45,821
Mr. Matlock, he had a lot of
phones and a ledger by his bed.

268
00:15:45,845 --> 00:15:48,357
I know he wasn't selling
magazine subscriptions.

269
00:15:48,381 --> 00:15:50,125
This ledger, you
know where it's at?

270
00:15:50,149 --> 00:15:51,360
I have no idea.

271
00:15:51,384 --> 00:15:54,163
It's in his office, I suppose.

272
00:15:54,187 --> 00:15:56,349
Listen, uh, you
can hang onto that.

273
00:15:59,158 --> 00:16:00,636
What a day.

274
00:16:00,660 --> 00:16:03,439
The guys I'm with,
I usually dump 'em,

275
00:16:03,463 --> 00:16:05,374
or they run back to their wives.

276
00:16:05,398 --> 00:16:07,075
No one's ever died on me before.

277
00:16:07,099 --> 00:16:10,512
It must be a shock.

278
00:16:10,536 --> 00:16:11,780
And, well, thank you.

279
00:16:11,804 --> 00:16:13,148
You've been a big help.

280
00:16:13,172 --> 00:16:14,800
Yeah.

281
00:16:22,748 --> 00:16:24,793
No, I'll tell you exactly
what I want, Norm:

282
00:16:24,817 --> 00:16:26,195
I want a signing bonus,

283
00:16:26,219 --> 00:16:27,429
I want a fair salary,

284
00:16:27,453 --> 00:16:28,797
and I want
performance incentives,

285
00:16:28,821 --> 00:16:31,500
and I want to know
today, you got that?

286
00:16:31,524 --> 00:16:33,135
No.

287
00:16:33,159 --> 00:16:34,536
That's a coffee stain.

288
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:36,605
No! Come on, Norm, you're
not even in the ballpark.

289
00:16:36,629 --> 00:16:37,606
Sit over here.

290
00:16:37,630 --> 00:16:38,707
Oh, sure.

291
00:16:38,731 --> 00:16:40,642
You want Hutchison
or not, yes or no?

292
00:16:40,666 --> 00:16:41,844
Can I get you anything?

293
00:16:41,868 --> 00:16:42,845
No, thank you.

294
00:16:42,869 --> 00:16:44,279
That <i>is</i> a coffee stain.

295
00:16:44,303 --> 00:16:47,850
No, no, Norm, <i>you</i>
don't understand.

296
00:16:47,874 --> 00:16:48,951
Tomorrow's too late.

297
00:16:48,975 --> 00:16:50,719
You got five minutes
to call me back

298
00:16:50,743 --> 00:16:52,554
or I'm on the phone
with the Raiders!

299
00:16:52,578 --> 00:16:53,722
You got that?!

300
00:16:54,947 --> 00:16:56,758
John Delaney. You
must be Ben Matlock.

301
00:16:56,782 --> 00:16:59,194
Yeah, I'm Ty Mullins' lawyer.

302
00:16:59,218 --> 00:17:00,311
Ah.

303
00:17:08,060 --> 00:17:10,529
Is that a... a bruise
on your chin?

304
00:17:12,298 --> 00:17:14,543
No, no, it's just a shadow.

305
00:17:14,567 --> 00:17:15,512
Just a shadow.

306
00:17:15,536 --> 00:17:16,912
I understand that, uh,

307
00:17:16,936 --> 00:17:20,582
that you and Eric
Gaston were great friends.

308
00:17:20,606 --> 00:17:21,650
Uh-huh, yeah.

309
00:17:21,674 --> 00:17:23,719
Played college
football with him.

310
00:17:23,743 --> 00:17:26,522
Eric was a star running
back, and I was his right tackle.

311
00:17:26,546 --> 00:17:28,590
Won the championship
my sophomore year.

312
00:17:28,614 --> 00:17:30,692
Hey, hey...

313
00:17:30,716 --> 00:17:34,630
Yeah, and I hear that you and a
couple other ex-football buddies

314
00:17:34,654 --> 00:17:38,600
were at his place the night
before he was murdered.

315
00:17:38,624 --> 00:17:40,569
Yeah, one of our
regular get-togethers.

316
00:17:40,593 --> 00:17:42,471
You know, a few
beers, a lot of laughs.

317
00:17:42,495 --> 00:17:45,374
Mostly bragging
about the glory days.

318
00:17:45,398 --> 00:17:47,776
Yeah, yeah, I guess so.

319
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:49,945
Did you know that
Eric was a bookie?

320
00:17:49,969 --> 00:17:51,713
Of course I did.

321
00:17:51,737 --> 00:17:54,249
Did you ever place
any bets with him?

322
00:17:54,273 --> 00:17:57,319
Gambling's for
losers, Mr. Matlock.

323
00:17:57,343 --> 00:18:01,657
Yeah... yeah,
you got that right.

324
00:18:01,681 --> 00:18:05,594
It still seem, seems
strange for a... a sports agent

325
00:18:05,618 --> 00:18:07,462
to be friends with a bookie.

326
00:18:07,486 --> 00:18:10,766
Did, uh, did he ever ask you

327
00:18:10,790 --> 00:18:12,267
for tips, you know,

328
00:18:12,291 --> 00:18:13,702
like who was injured
and who wasn't?

329
00:18:13,726 --> 00:18:14,803
No.

330
00:18:14,827 --> 00:18:16,939
I mean, a bookie
would pay big money

331
00:18:16,963 --> 00:18:18,607
for that kind of information.

332
00:18:18,631 --> 00:18:20,309
I said he never asked.

333
00:18:20,333 --> 00:18:21,977
S-Somebody told me

334
00:18:22,001 --> 00:18:25,013
that, that you and he
almost came to blows

335
00:18:25,037 --> 00:18:27,516
at his club a couple years ago.

336
00:18:27,540 --> 00:18:29,084
It was over a girl.

337
00:18:29,108 --> 00:18:30,218
Oh, don't tell me.

338
00:18:30,242 --> 00:18:31,720
Next question
you're gonna ask is

339
00:18:31,744 --> 00:18:33,922
where was I at the
time of the murder, right?

340
00:18:33,946 --> 00:18:35,090
It wouldn't hurt.

341
00:18:35,114 --> 00:18:36,658
I was right here.

342
00:18:38,184 --> 00:18:40,228
Yeah. Delaney.

343
00:18:40,252 --> 00:18:41,830
Yeah, Norm.

344
00:18:41,854 --> 00:18:45,167
No. No.

345
00:18:45,191 --> 00:18:48,437
No, I can't give him
those figures, Norm.

346
00:18:48,461 --> 00:18:51,989
That insults me, you know that?

347
00:19:06,278 --> 00:19:07,656
Quick, where's the kitchen?

348
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:08,991
This sucker's heavy.

349
00:19:09,015 --> 00:19:13,395
Ty, what... what in the
world have you got in there?!

350
00:19:13,419 --> 00:19:14,663
Supper.

351
00:19:14,687 --> 00:19:15,664
You're kidding.

352
00:19:15,688 --> 00:19:16,865
Yeah, boy.

353
00:19:16,889 --> 00:19:18,567
- Ooh, and it's still hot, too.
- Ah...!

354
00:19:18,591 --> 00:19:20,302
Well, don't just
stand there, man.

355
00:19:20,326 --> 00:19:22,604
Go get us some
plates and silverware!

356
00:19:22,628 --> 00:19:25,007
You don't want to eat
Morocco-style, do you?

357
00:19:29,001 --> 00:19:30,545
Mmm-mmm-mmm.

358
00:19:30,569 --> 00:19:34,016
Mmm... mmm-mmm-mmm!

359
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:37,119
Ah! Whew! Boy, I'm full as Dick.

360
00:19:37,143 --> 00:19:38,286
Whew!

361
00:19:38,310 --> 00:19:40,055
You eat like this all the time?

362
00:19:40,079 --> 00:19:42,391
You don't think I got this
way eating salads, do you?

363
00:19:43,949 --> 00:19:46,428
Now what-what-what's
some of this stuff called?

364
00:19:46,452 --> 00:19:48,363
Let's see here.

365
00:19:48,387 --> 00:19:52,567
Uh, well, this one was called
"Evelyn Walters' Never Fail

366
00:19:52,591 --> 00:19:54,136
Sunday Baked Chicken."

367
00:19:54,160 --> 00:19:55,470
We had a little bit of

368
00:19:55,494 --> 00:19:59,341
Rebecca Venerable's
sauerkraut salad,

369
00:19:59,365 --> 00:20:00,609
and last but not least,

370
00:20:00,633 --> 00:20:04,146
whew, Goldie's
Yo-Yo pudding. Ooh!

371
00:20:04,170 --> 00:20:06,682
Yeah, outstanding.

372
00:20:06,706 --> 00:20:07,749
All of 'em outstanding.

373
00:20:07,773 --> 00:20:09,584
Let me help you
clean up this mess.

374
00:20:09,608 --> 00:20:11,386
No, no, no, leave
it. I'll get that.

375
00:20:11,410 --> 00:20:12,754
Let's go in, let's go in

376
00:20:12,778 --> 00:20:14,823
the other room and
hear a little tune.

377
00:20:14,847 --> 00:20:16,358
You got it.

378
00:20:16,382 --> 00:20:17,782
Go on in here.

379
00:20:18,951 --> 00:20:20,729
Ty, I don't pretend

380
00:20:20,753 --> 00:20:22,698
to know much about
compulsive gambling,

381
00:20:22,722 --> 00:20:24,866
but from now on,
you're not to as much

382
00:20:24,890 --> 00:20:27,335
as buy a lottery
ticket, you understand?

383
00:20:27,359 --> 00:20:28,336
I understand.

384
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:29,371
Okay.

385
00:20:29,395 --> 00:20:33,475
Uh, did, uh, Eric
Gaston have a ledger?

386
00:20:33,499 --> 00:20:35,944
Yeah, he kept it
in his top drawer

387
00:20:35,968 --> 00:20:37,579
in the desk at the club.

388
00:20:37,603 --> 00:20:39,514
It's not there.

389
00:20:39,538 --> 00:20:41,016
How long was he a bookie?

390
00:20:41,040 --> 00:20:42,617
Said it's something
he learned in college.

391
00:20:42,641 --> 00:20:44,419
In college?!

392
00:20:44,443 --> 00:20:45,787
Play it much?

393
00:20:45,811 --> 00:20:47,489
No, no, not much, no.

394
00:20:47,513 --> 00:20:48,590
That's a shame.

395
00:20:48,614 --> 00:20:50,559
You know, these
things are like women;

396
00:20:50,583 --> 00:20:53,095
they like to be stroked
from time to time.

397
00:21:12,605 --> 00:21:17,252
♪ There is a house ♪

398
00:21:17,276 --> 00:21:21,957
♪ Down in New Orleans ♪

399
00:21:21,981 --> 00:21:28,444
♪ They call the Rising Sun ♪

400
00:21:31,023 --> 00:21:34,236
♪ Well, it's been the ruins ♪

401
00:21:34,260 --> 00:21:37,890
♪ Of a... many a poor boy ♪

402
00:21:39,732 --> 00:21:45,433
♪ And, God, I know I'm one ♪

403
00:21:48,507 --> 00:21:51,419
♪ Mamas ♪

404
00:21:51,443 --> 00:21:56,057
♪ Tell your children ♪

405
00:21:56,081 --> 00:22:01,520
♪ Not to do as I have done ♪

406
00:22:03,823 --> 00:22:08,436
♪ And shun the house ♪

407
00:22:08,460 --> 00:22:11,573
♪ Down in New Orleans ♪

408
00:22:11,597 --> 00:22:19,281
♪ The house they
call the Rising... ♪

409
00:22:19,305 --> 00:22:21,716
♪ Sun. ♪

410
00:22:28,747 --> 00:22:30,392
All right!

411
00:22:30,416 --> 00:22:32,460
Good!

412
00:23:04,516 --> 00:23:07,562
Hello, John. What do you have?

413
00:23:07,586 --> 00:23:09,464
Where's your wife?

414
00:23:09,488 --> 00:23:11,967
She's over in Linville
visiting her mother... why?

415
00:23:11,991 --> 00:23:14,790
I just want to make
sure we're alone.

416
00:23:16,462 --> 00:23:18,658
So which one of you did it?

417
00:23:20,099 --> 00:23:22,377
Wait a minute... you
think one of us killed Eric?

418
00:23:22,401 --> 00:23:24,112
All I know is Ben
Matlock thinks I killed Eric.

419
00:23:24,136 --> 00:23:25,680
Now, just who the hell
am I protecting here?

420
00:23:25,704 --> 00:23:26,848
Well, hell, we
thought you killed him!

421
00:23:26,872 --> 00:23:28,116
Would you guys cool it?

422
00:23:28,140 --> 00:23:29,751
That is not why I
brought you here.

423
00:23:29,775 --> 00:23:30,775
We've got a problem.

424
00:23:33,145 --> 00:23:35,423
Hi, Tom. This is Sherry.

425
00:23:35,447 --> 00:23:39,194
Bet you, Roy and John
think it's all over, huh?

426
00:23:39,218 --> 00:23:40,962
Well, surprise.

427
00:23:40,986 --> 00:23:42,931
Guess who has you know what?

428
00:23:42,955 --> 00:23:45,367
I was just gonna turn
'em over to the police,

429
00:23:45,391 --> 00:23:48,236
but then, I thought, I can't
do that to such sexy guys.

430
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:50,405
So, fellas, they're yours.

431
00:23:50,429 --> 00:23:52,407
For 50 grand apiece.

432
00:23:52,431 --> 00:23:54,209
Think it over.

433
00:23:54,233 --> 00:23:55,233
Call me tomorrow.

434
00:23:58,304 --> 00:23:59,681
Who the hell is Sherry?

435
00:23:59,705 --> 00:24:00,949
That's that blonde bimbo

436
00:24:00,973 --> 00:24:02,417
that was always hanging
around Eric at the club.

437
00:24:02,441 --> 00:24:03,718
When'd she call?

438
00:24:03,742 --> 00:24:05,553
She called me this
morning on my private line.

439
00:24:05,577 --> 00:24:07,155
And you <i>wish</i> she
was a bimbo, John.

440
00:24:07,179 --> 00:24:08,924
She... is smart.

441
00:24:08,948 --> 00:24:10,507
And dangerous.

442
00:24:26,865 --> 00:24:28,777
Sorry I kept you waiting.

443
00:24:28,801 --> 00:24:30,512
I had a late night.

444
00:24:30,536 --> 00:24:32,869
Uh, that-that-that's okay.

445
00:24:33,906 --> 00:24:35,984
Have you got the key?

446
00:24:36,008 --> 00:24:37,374
Right here.

447
00:24:54,560 --> 00:24:58,573
Well... where else can we look?

448
00:24:58,597 --> 00:25:00,709
Beats me.

449
00:25:00,733 --> 00:25:02,777
Maybe the kitchen?

450
00:25:02,801 --> 00:25:05,430
Well, I-I've never
been in the kitchen.

451
00:25:07,206 --> 00:25:09,985
It wasn't my cooking
that turned Eric on.

452
00:25:10,009 --> 00:25:11,671
Oh.

453
00:25:13,379 --> 00:25:16,624
I'm beginning to
believe it's not here.

454
00:25:16,648 --> 00:25:19,928
<i>So, where do you
think</i> the ledger is?

455
00:25:19,952 --> 00:25:22,230
Well, whoever killed
Eric has it, I guess.

456
00:25:22,254 --> 00:25:24,632
Or had it, or... maybe
it's destroyed by now.

457
00:25:24,656 --> 00:25:25,800
Who knows?

458
00:25:25,824 --> 00:25:27,402
Well, thanks for coming over...

459
00:25:45,210 --> 00:25:47,188
Do they know what happened?

460
00:25:47,212 --> 00:25:48,523
Drunk driver, my eye.

461
00:25:48,547 --> 00:25:49,958
That car was
heading right for us.

462
00:25:49,982 --> 00:25:51,359
You all right?

463
00:25:51,383 --> 00:25:53,228
Yeah, I'm okay. I'm
just a little shaken up.

464
00:25:53,252 --> 00:25:54,462
I'm gonna get going, okay?

465
00:25:54,486 --> 00:25:55,697
Yeah, go ahead, go ahead.

466
00:25:55,721 --> 00:25:57,899
You didn't get a
good look at the driver.

467
00:25:57,923 --> 00:25:59,167
Nor the license plate.

468
00:25:59,191 --> 00:26:01,102
But you're sure it's
one of the suspects.

469
00:26:01,126 --> 00:26:03,271
Or somebody they hired.
Who else could it be?

470
00:26:03,295 --> 00:26:05,707
But you don't have anything
on any of the suspects.

471
00:26:05,731 --> 00:26:07,042
Why would anybody bother?

472
00:26:07,066 --> 00:26:09,110
Maybe they think I
got something on 'em.

473
00:26:09,134 --> 00:26:12,213
Or maybe I got something
on 'em and don't know it yet.

474
00:26:12,237 --> 00:26:14,816
Think it'll run?

475
00:26:14,840 --> 00:26:17,385
Yeah, sure, with a
tow truck pulling it.

476
00:26:19,511 --> 00:26:21,673
Bad joke.

477
00:26:39,965 --> 00:26:41,543
Sherry?

478
00:26:43,368 --> 00:26:45,462
Want me to give you a lift?

479
00:26:46,672 --> 00:26:48,683
No, no, I'm-I'm-I'm fine.

480
00:27:05,057 --> 00:27:06,457
Hut!

481
00:27:09,828 --> 00:27:12,507
Now in their 25th
year, the Baxter Falcons

482
00:27:12,531 --> 00:27:14,342
are celebrating a
silver anniversary.

483
00:27:14,366 --> 00:27:16,578
Coming off of what
has to be considered

484
00:27:16,602 --> 00:27:18,780
their worst year ever,
the Falcons are attempting

485
00:27:18,804 --> 00:27:20,482
- to bring...
- Roy Stevens!

486
00:27:20,506 --> 00:27:22,684
Cut, cut.

487
00:27:22,708 --> 00:27:25,753
Oh, whoa, you're not
live or anything, are you?

488
00:27:25,777 --> 00:27:28,941
No, no. If we were,
I'd be screaming now.

489
00:27:33,118 --> 00:27:35,730
You were a friend of
Eric Gaston's, right?

490
00:27:35,754 --> 00:27:37,031
That's right.

491
00:27:37,055 --> 00:27:38,867
Played football with
him at Baxter University.

492
00:27:38,891 --> 00:27:42,303
As a matter of fact, me and
two other old friends of his

493
00:27:42,327 --> 00:27:45,039
were at the nightclub
the night before he died.

494
00:27:45,063 --> 00:27:46,341
Doing what?

495
00:27:46,365 --> 00:27:49,344
Well, you know, a couple
of drinks, a few laughs.

496
00:27:49,368 --> 00:27:52,770
Like I said, uh, we
were old friends.

497
00:27:54,740 --> 00:27:56,718
Excuse me, what, uh,

498
00:27:56,742 --> 00:27:58,419
what do you keep staring at?

499
00:27:58,443 --> 00:28:01,256
Oh, that's right,
you're wearing makeup.

500
00:28:01,280 --> 00:28:03,658
Of course I'm wearing
makeup; I'm doing a show.

501
00:28:03,682 --> 00:28:06,528
I'll bet sometimes
that comes in handy.

502
00:28:06,552 --> 00:28:09,797
You cut yourself shaving,
nobody'd notice, huh?

503
00:28:09,821 --> 00:28:11,699
Yeah, yeah, I guess so.

504
00:28:11,723 --> 00:28:14,989
You ever place bets with Eric?

505
00:28:16,595 --> 00:28:18,406
Yeah, yeah, we all did.

506
00:28:18,430 --> 00:28:19,908
You owe him money when he died?

507
00:28:19,932 --> 00:28:21,242
No.

508
00:28:21,266 --> 00:28:23,244
And I don't appreciate
what you're implying.

509
00:28:23,268 --> 00:28:25,613
I told you Eric
and I were friends.

510
00:28:25,637 --> 00:28:27,081
Even friends have arguments.

511
00:28:27,105 --> 00:28:29,751
Yeah, well, we didn't.

512
00:28:29,775 --> 00:28:31,219
Besides, I, uh...

513
00:28:31,243 --> 00:28:34,289
I was taping my interview with
the coach of the Atlanta Falcons

514
00:28:34,313 --> 00:28:36,090
on the morning
that Eric was killed.

515
00:28:36,114 --> 00:28:39,027
We started in at 9:30, and
we finished taping at 10:30.

516
00:28:39,051 --> 00:28:40,828
You don't believe
me, you ask him.

517
00:28:40,852 --> 00:28:42,697
He'll tell you.

518
00:28:42,721 --> 00:28:47,220
Now, if you don't
mind... Excuse me.

519
00:29:00,138 --> 00:29:01,783
Excuse me.

520
00:29:01,807 --> 00:29:03,117
Martin Kravetz?

521
00:29:03,141 --> 00:29:04,452
That's right.

522
00:29:04,476 --> 00:29:06,454
How you doing? I'm
Conrad McMasters.

523
00:29:06,478 --> 00:29:07,488
Uh-huh.

524
00:29:07,512 --> 00:29:09,504
Private investigator.

525
00:29:12,351 --> 00:29:15,185
All right, Jubal, that
ought to hold you.

526
00:29:16,221 --> 00:29:18,132
A real private eye, huh?

527
00:29:18,156 --> 00:29:20,134
Yeah.

528
00:29:20,158 --> 00:29:22,403
You remember Eric Gaston?

529
00:29:22,427 --> 00:29:23,972
Yeah, I sure do.

530
00:29:23,996 --> 00:29:25,840
Best running back
this school's ever seen.

531
00:29:25,864 --> 00:29:27,842
It's no surprise whatever
happened to him.

532
00:29:27,866 --> 00:29:29,477
Why do you say that?

533
00:29:29,501 --> 00:29:31,779
Eric was always in trouble.

534
00:29:31,803 --> 00:29:34,148
He only played by one
set of rules: his own.

535
00:29:34,172 --> 00:29:36,084
That's what got him
kicked out of here.

536
00:29:36,108 --> 00:29:37,585
He got kicked off
the football team?

537
00:29:37,609 --> 00:29:39,053
No, he was kicked out of school.

538
00:29:39,077 --> 00:29:40,755
Expelled in the middle
of his senior year.

539
00:29:40,779 --> 00:29:42,957
Why did they expel
him from school?

540
00:29:42,981 --> 00:29:44,325
Gambling.

541
00:29:44,349 --> 00:29:47,395
Yeah, he was putting money
on Baxter football games.

542
00:29:47,419 --> 00:29:49,163
He would bet on
the opposing team,

543
00:29:49,187 --> 00:29:51,366
then he would manipulate
the point spread

544
00:29:51,390 --> 00:29:54,502
by faking an injury or taking
himself out of the game.

545
00:29:54,526 --> 00:29:57,372
Kid was just too damn
smart for his own good.

546
00:29:57,396 --> 00:29:59,874
Do you remember John Delaney?

547
00:29:59,898 --> 00:30:01,075
Delaney.

548
00:30:01,099 --> 00:30:03,745
Yeah, yeah, he
played right tackle.

549
00:30:03,769 --> 00:30:06,447
What about Tom
Hermanski and Roy Stevens?

550
00:30:06,471 --> 00:30:07,915
Wide receiver and noseguard.

551
00:30:07,939 --> 00:30:09,250
What about 'em?

552
00:30:09,274 --> 00:30:11,319
Were they involved
in the gambling, too?

553
00:30:11,343 --> 00:30:12,420
No, no. Just Gaston.

554
00:30:12,444 --> 00:30:13,955
If the other guys
were, I'd remember.

555
00:30:13,979 --> 00:30:16,124
I'm sure you would.

556
00:30:16,148 --> 00:30:18,660
Okay. Thank you, Mr. Kravetz.

557
00:30:18,684 --> 00:30:20,016
Yeah.

558
00:30:33,598 --> 00:30:36,611
He made my heart
stop out there today.

559
00:30:36,635 --> 00:30:38,646
Ran his best time ever.

560
00:30:38,670 --> 00:30:40,748
Uh, Mr. Hermanski?

561
00:30:40,772 --> 00:30:42,116
Uh, hi.

562
00:30:42,140 --> 00:30:44,886
I'm, uh, Ben Matlock,
Ty Mullins' lawyer.

563
00:30:44,910 --> 00:30:46,554
Oh, good to meet you.

564
00:30:46,578 --> 00:30:48,122
Your wife told me
you were back here.

565
00:30:48,146 --> 00:30:49,490
Said you were expecting me.

566
00:30:49,514 --> 00:30:52,026
John Delaney and Roy
Stevens said you'd show up.

567
00:30:52,050 --> 00:30:56,130
Uh, John, Roy, Eric and
me... Friends from way back.

568
00:30:56,154 --> 00:30:57,332
I've heard that.

569
00:30:57,356 --> 00:30:58,466
You ever come face-to-face

570
00:30:58,490 --> 00:31:00,201
with a Triple Crown
winner before?

571
00:31:00,225 --> 00:31:02,570
Won the Triple Crown?

572
00:31:02,594 --> 00:31:04,972
Not yet, but he will.

573
00:31:04,996 --> 00:31:07,742
Lot of money to
be made in horses.

574
00:31:07,766 --> 00:31:11,713
A lot to be spent, but...
a whole lot to be made.

575
00:31:11,737 --> 00:31:14,282
You mean racing
them or selling them

576
00:31:14,306 --> 00:31:15,917
or betting on them?

577
00:31:15,941 --> 00:31:18,786
All three.

578
00:31:18,810 --> 00:31:21,622
Did you ever place
any bets with Eric?

579
00:31:21,646 --> 00:31:23,424
Oh, sure.

580
00:31:23,448 --> 00:31:27,442
Maybe, uh, you owed him
money or he owed... you money?

581
00:31:29,020 --> 00:31:31,833
I had no reason to
kill Eric, Mr. Matlock.

582
00:31:31,857 --> 00:31:33,568
Mr. Hermanski!

583
00:31:33,592 --> 00:31:35,103
Telephone!

584
00:31:35,127 --> 00:31:36,571
All right.

585
00:31:36,595 --> 00:31:38,740
What's more, I
couldn't have killed him.

586
00:31:38,764 --> 00:31:41,743
I lift weights every
morning from 9:00 to 10:00.

587
00:31:41,767 --> 00:31:42,944
Here?

588
00:31:42,968 --> 00:31:45,301
Lloyd's Gym. If
you'll excuse me.

589
00:31:53,278 --> 00:31:54,622
Tom Hermanski.

590
00:31:54,646 --> 00:31:57,158
That was really stupid, Tom.

591
00:31:57,182 --> 00:31:58,526
Who is this?

592
00:31:58,550 --> 00:31:59,727
Sherry.

593
00:31:59,751 --> 00:32:01,629
The woman you
just tried to run over.

594
00:32:01,653 --> 00:32:02,964
What are you talking about?

595
00:32:02,988 --> 00:32:05,767
That's gonna cost you
guys an extra 25 grand.

596
00:32:05,791 --> 00:32:06,934
Now, just a minute.

597
00:32:06,958 --> 00:32:08,569
That makes $75,000 apiece,

598
00:32:08,593 --> 00:32:10,037
and I want it tomorrow.

599
00:32:10,061 --> 00:32:11,439
You're out of your mind.

600
00:32:11,463 --> 00:32:12,640
That's impossible.

601
00:32:12,664 --> 00:32:14,108
Well, I hope not, for your sake.

602
00:32:14,132 --> 00:32:16,010
I want you to bring
the money, in cash,

603
00:32:16,034 --> 00:32:18,546
to the Sky View Lounge at
the airport tomorrow at 1:00.

604
00:32:18,570 --> 00:32:20,515
Now, Tom, if the
cash isn't all there,

605
00:32:20,539 --> 00:32:23,451
or if you bring company, you
guys are in the evening edition.

606
00:32:23,475 --> 00:32:25,019
And you can bet on it!

607
00:32:36,121 --> 00:32:37,398
Rogers drives
through the center,

608
00:32:37,422 --> 00:32:39,600
and there's the tackle
on the 44 yard line.

609
00:32:39,624 --> 00:32:41,769
A gain of two
yards on that play.

610
00:32:41,793 --> 00:32:43,304
Third down, seven to go.

611
00:32:51,837 --> 00:32:53,314
Oh, hi, Ben.

612
00:32:53,338 --> 00:32:55,483
Got your message. What's up?

613
00:32:55,507 --> 00:32:59,000
I just looked into something
that's gonna help the case.

614
00:33:00,178 --> 00:33:01,889
That's Frankie Lance over there.

615
00:33:01,913 --> 00:33:03,724
- I know.
- He's a bookie.

616
00:33:03,748 --> 00:33:05,760
I know. I just talked
to him a minute ago.

617
00:33:05,784 --> 00:33:07,862
I don't want to hear that.

618
00:33:07,886 --> 00:33:10,031
I didn't place a bet, Ben.

619
00:33:10,055 --> 00:33:14,001
Frankie just told me that Eric
was into a couple of loan sharks

620
00:33:14,025 --> 00:33:15,870
for 150 grand.

621
00:33:15,894 --> 00:33:17,238
How did it happen?

622
00:33:17,262 --> 00:33:19,474
Apparently, he took a
whuppin' last weekend

623
00:33:19,498 --> 00:33:20,875
on a couple of games.

624
00:33:20,899 --> 00:33:23,110
They been putting the
squeeze on him real hard.

625
00:33:23,134 --> 00:33:25,947
Maybe he wanted to
squeeze somebody back.

626
00:33:25,971 --> 00:33:27,949
Hmm.

627
00:33:27,973 --> 00:33:29,784
Touchdown?

628
00:33:29,808 --> 00:33:32,920
I told you I knew the
Green Bay Packers!

629
00:33:32,944 --> 00:33:35,072
Oh, yeah!

630
00:33:39,751 --> 00:33:41,462
Five bucks, Ben.

631
00:33:41,486 --> 00:33:43,887
It's... It's not even a bet!

632
00:33:56,635 --> 00:33:58,479
Flight to New York passenger

633
00:33:58,503 --> 00:34:02,383
Alberto Robinson
please report to Gate 12.

634
00:34:02,407 --> 00:34:05,253
New York passenger Alberto
Robinson please report...

635
00:34:05,277 --> 00:34:08,589
Excuse me, sir, I believe
this belongs to me.

636
00:34:08,613 --> 00:34:10,892
Aren't you forgetting something?

637
00:34:10,916 --> 00:34:12,193
You'll get the negatives

638
00:34:12,217 --> 00:34:14,829
when I'm sure there's
$225,000 in here.

639
00:34:14,853 --> 00:34:15,830
That wasn't our deal.

640
00:34:15,854 --> 00:34:17,220
Sorry.

641
00:34:19,224 --> 00:34:21,420
I'll call you tonight.

642
00:34:31,269 --> 00:34:33,247
<i>♪ Like Jack Horner ♪</i>

643
00:34:33,271 --> 00:34:35,249
♪ In the corner ♪

644
00:34:35,273 --> 00:34:37,018
♪ Don't go nowhere ♪

645
00:34:37,042 --> 00:34:38,853
♪ What do I care? ♪

646
00:34:38,877 --> 00:34:40,655
♪ Your kisses ♪

647
00:34:40,679 --> 00:34:43,291
♪ Are worth waiting for ♪

648
00:34:43,315 --> 00:34:45,626
♪ Oh, believe me ♪

649
00:34:45,650 --> 00:34:47,929
♪ I don't stay out late ♪

650
00:34:47,953 --> 00:34:49,830
♪ Don't care to go ♪

651
00:34:49,854 --> 00:34:51,299
♪ I'm home about eight ♪

652
00:34:51,323 --> 00:34:53,935
♪ Just me and my radio ♪

653
00:34:53,959 --> 00:34:55,503
♪ Ain't misbehavin' ♪

654
00:34:55,527 --> 00:34:58,497
♪ I'm saving my love for you ♪

655
00:34:59,531 --> 00:35:02,009
♪ Ain't misbehavin' ♪

656
00:35:02,033 --> 00:35:06,147
♪ I'm saving my love for you ♪

657
00:35:06,171 --> 00:35:07,448
♪ Oh, yeah! ♪

658
00:35:09,841 --> 00:35:12,019
All right! All right!

659
00:35:12,043 --> 00:35:13,487
That's the way!

660
00:35:13,511 --> 00:35:16,257
Good! You know, you
don't have to bring food

661
00:35:16,281 --> 00:35:17,925
every time you come over here.

662
00:35:17,949 --> 00:35:19,160
I enjoy it.

663
00:35:19,184 --> 00:35:20,394
You like that?

664
00:35:20,418 --> 00:35:22,363
Yeah, it's good.
What's it called again?

665
00:35:22,387 --> 00:35:24,432
Aunt Bessie's sweet potato pie.

666
00:35:24,456 --> 00:35:27,435
You know, they say that when
Aunt Bessie's husband died,

667
00:35:27,459 --> 00:35:29,770
she baked a pie
and put it in the coffin.

668
00:35:29,794 --> 00:35:31,372
- She did?
- Oh, yeah.

669
00:35:31,396 --> 00:35:33,541
She was very classy;
went all the way.

670
00:35:33,565 --> 00:35:35,676
She put in a... a linen napkin,

671
00:35:35,700 --> 00:35:37,745
dental floss and mouthwash.

672
00:35:37,769 --> 00:35:39,780
But, of course, he had to eat it

673
00:35:39,804 --> 00:35:41,782
from a paper plate
with a plastic fork.

674
00:35:41,806 --> 00:35:43,484
But it was the thought.

675
00:35:43,508 --> 00:35:46,487
I'll be, I'll get me some
more before my turn.

676
00:36:16,141 --> 00:36:18,736
♪♪

677
00:36:30,221 --> 00:36:33,601
Hey, man, I didn't tell
you; we got a gig Saturday.

678
00:36:33,625 --> 00:36:35,169
And you won't ever guess where.

679
00:36:35,193 --> 00:36:36,504
Where?

680
00:36:36,528 --> 00:36:38,906
Gaston's Blues Club.

681
00:36:38,930 --> 00:36:40,641
New owner called me today.

682
00:36:40,665 --> 00:36:42,143
Isn't that the irony for you?

683
00:36:42,167 --> 00:36:44,345
Me playing at a club
that used to be owned

684
00:36:44,369 --> 00:36:46,147
by the guy I'm on
trial for murdering.

685
00:36:46,171 --> 00:36:47,171
Yeah.

686
00:36:52,343 --> 00:36:53,709
Hmm.

687
00:36:55,714 --> 00:36:57,080
Where'd this come from?

688
00:36:58,783 --> 00:37:01,062
Oh, man, you
spoiled my surprise.

689
00:37:01,086 --> 00:37:03,030
That's the first payment
for your services.

690
00:37:03,054 --> 00:37:05,466
You didn't answer my question.

691
00:37:05,490 --> 00:37:06,801
Yeah, where I get it from.

692
00:37:06,825 --> 00:37:09,804
Um, man, my folks
they're so great.

693
00:37:09,828 --> 00:37:11,472
When they found
out I was in prison,

694
00:37:11,496 --> 00:37:12,540
they sent over ten grand.

695
00:37:12,564 --> 00:37:15,209
They mailed you cash?

696
00:37:15,233 --> 00:37:16,243
No, no.

697
00:37:16,267 --> 00:37:18,379
They sent, uh, a
check, which I-I cashed

698
00:37:18,403 --> 00:37:20,548
because it was under
my name and all.

699
00:37:20,572 --> 00:37:22,370
Uh-huh.

700
00:37:24,309 --> 00:37:26,153
You been gambling?

701
00:37:26,177 --> 00:37:28,589
No, Ben.

702
00:37:28,613 --> 00:37:30,024
I told you I'd stop.

703
00:37:30,048 --> 00:37:31,726
Answer my question.

704
00:37:31,750 --> 00:37:33,594
No!

705
00:37:33,618 --> 00:37:36,144
It's from my folks, honest.

706
00:37:39,424 --> 00:37:43,170
Ty... you got to do
something for me.

707
00:37:43,194 --> 00:37:44,890
Anything, Ben.

708
00:37:46,598 --> 00:37:48,743
Tell your folks I
said thank you.

709
00:37:49,768 --> 00:37:52,379
I'll do that.

710
00:37:52,403 --> 00:37:54,668
Play something.

711
00:38:30,775 --> 00:38:31,936
Sherry?

712
00:39:18,990 --> 00:39:21,735
Tattoo, huh?

713
00:39:21,759 --> 00:39:24,238
He... He had a tattoo?

714
00:39:24,262 --> 00:39:26,740
No, he had two tattoos
on-on-on either forearm.

715
00:39:26,764 --> 00:39:27,808
Huh.

716
00:39:27,832 --> 00:39:29,109
Some kind of
flowers or something.

717
00:39:29,133 --> 00:39:32,913
About six foot, 190
pounds, dark hair?

718
00:39:32,937 --> 00:39:34,248
Yeah, how'd you know that?

719
00:39:34,272 --> 00:39:36,517
Sounds like a guy that
works for Tom Hermanski.

720
00:39:36,541 --> 00:39:38,032
I saw him out at the ranch.

721
00:39:40,078 --> 00:39:42,323
I think they're looking
for Eric's ledger.

722
00:39:42,347 --> 00:39:45,442
They're looking for something.

723
00:39:52,557 --> 00:39:53,868
Sorry to keep you waiting,

724
00:39:53,892 --> 00:39:55,836
but I had no idea
you'd be dropping by.

725
00:39:55,860 --> 00:39:56,837
Oh, that's okay.

726
00:39:56,861 --> 00:39:58,439
I didn't know I was coming over.

727
00:39:58,463 --> 00:40:01,208
Il just got to thinking
about, uh, Sherry Brown

728
00:40:01,232 --> 00:40:04,144
and wondering why your
man broke into her house.

729
00:40:04,168 --> 00:40:05,913
What are you talking about?

730
00:40:05,937 --> 00:40:08,582
Are you and your two football
buddies in on this together

731
00:40:08,606 --> 00:40:10,684
or were you acting on your own?

732
00:40:10,708 --> 00:40:12,319
You've totally lost me, okay?

733
00:40:12,343 --> 00:40:14,455
Uh, you married well.

734
00:40:14,479 --> 00:40:16,790
Your wife could've given
you the money to pay Eric off.

735
00:40:16,814 --> 00:40:17,892
Why kill him?

736
00:40:17,916 --> 00:40:20,828
Look, I don't
have time for this.

737
00:40:20,852 --> 00:40:23,163
I should've gone to
the police first, I guess,

738
00:40:23,187 --> 00:40:25,032
but I thought I'd
give you a crack at it.

739
00:40:25,056 --> 00:40:26,066
Get out.

740
00:40:26,090 --> 00:40:28,502
Well, okay, if that's
the way you want it.

741
00:40:28,526 --> 00:40:30,671
But I'll just have to come
back with a subpoena.

742
00:40:30,695 --> 00:40:33,140
Maybe bring the
police with a warrant.

743
00:40:33,164 --> 00:40:35,156
That's fine. I'll
take my chances.

744
00:41:01,392 --> 00:41:02,636
It's me.

745
00:41:02,660 --> 00:41:05,755
The three of us
have got to talk now.

746
00:41:23,948 --> 00:41:26,593
Lot number 14 on your
program, ladies and gentlemen.

747
00:41:26,617 --> 00:41:28,595
A fine piece of horseflesh
and it has a chance

748
00:41:28,619 --> 00:41:30,431
to make you some
good money on the track.

749
00:41:30,455 --> 00:41:32,700
4,000, now 4,500.
Will you bet 4,500?

750
00:41:32,724 --> 00:41:35,436
Will you bet 4,500? Will
you bet 4,500! Now five.

751
00:41:35,460 --> 00:41:37,171
4,500, now 5,000.
Will you bet 5,000?

752
00:41:37,195 --> 00:41:38,872
Will you bet 5,000?
Will you make it 5,000?

753
00:41:38,896 --> 00:41:41,375
5,000! Now six.
5,000, now 6,000.

754
00:41:41,399 --> 00:41:42,876
Will you bet 6,000?
Will you bet 6,000?

755
00:41:42,900 --> 00:41:44,611
Will you bet six thou...
Will you bet 6,000?

756
00:41:44,635 --> 00:41:46,780
5,000 now 6,000! Now 6,500.

757
00:41:46,804 --> 00:41:48,215
6,000, now 6,500.

758
00:41:48,239 --> 00:41:49,984
Will you bet 6,500?
Will you bet 6,500?

759
00:41:50,008 --> 00:41:51,885
Will you bet 6,500?
Will you bet 65

760
00:41:51,909 --> 00:41:54,054
6,500, now 7,000.

761
00:41:54,078 --> 00:41:55,255
$6,500 bet, now 7,000.

762
00:41:55,279 --> 00:41:56,924
Will you bet 7,000?
Will you bet 7,000?

763
00:41:56,948 --> 00:41:59,259
Will you make it 7,000?
Will you bet 7,000, now 7,500.

764
00:41:59,283 --> 00:42:02,262
What do you mean,
Matlock knows something?

765
00:42:02,286 --> 00:42:05,666
He knows that somebody
ransacked Sherry's place.

766
00:42:05,690 --> 00:42:06,934
Somebody working for me.

767
00:42:06,958 --> 00:42:09,052
Did he find the negatives?

768
00:42:10,228 --> 00:42:11,805
Great.

769
00:42:11,829 --> 00:42:14,708
Well, did that crazy broad
tell him what the guy was after?

770
00:42:14,732 --> 00:42:16,343
What are you, stupid?

771
00:42:16,367 --> 00:42:19,146
Eric had those negatives
for 15 years and she knows it.

772
00:42:19,170 --> 00:42:21,015
Yeah.

773
00:42:21,039 --> 00:42:22,950
No, she's not gonna
tell anybody about them

774
00:42:22,974 --> 00:42:24,618
until she's milked us bone dry.

775
00:42:24,642 --> 00:42:26,854
Yeah, well, I
can't get any drier.

776
00:42:26,878 --> 00:42:28,622
One more payment
to her and I'm finished.

777
00:42:28,646 --> 00:42:29,623
Me, too.

778
00:42:29,647 --> 00:42:35,195
So... what are we gonna do?

779
00:42:35,219 --> 00:42:36,930
Whatever it takes.

780
00:42:36,954 --> 00:42:39,066
You think about it.

781
00:42:39,090 --> 00:42:40,067
Let's talk tonight, huh?

782
00:42:40,091 --> 00:42:41,201
Yeah.

783
00:42:41,225 --> 00:42:43,670
Buyer number 84,
thank you very much, sir.

784
00:42:43,694 --> 00:42:46,373
Lot number 15 on your
program, ladies and gentlemen.

785
00:42:46,397 --> 00:42:48,275
A really fine piece
of horseflesh.

786
00:42:48,299 --> 00:42:50,310
8,500, now 9,000.
Will you bet 9,000?

787
00:42:50,334 --> 00:42:52,780
Will you bet 9,000?
9,000! Now 9,500.

788
00:42:52,804 --> 00:42:54,681
$9,000 bid, now 9,500.

789
00:42:54,705 --> 00:42:55,849
9,500, now 10,000.

790
00:42:55,873 --> 00:42:58,485
$9,500 bet, now 10,000.
Will you bet 10,000?

791
00:42:58,509 --> 00:42:59,887
I have 10,000!

792
00:42:59,911 --> 00:43:01,188
Will I have ten-five?

793
00:43:01,212 --> 00:43:02,589
I have 10,000. Will
you bet ten-five?

794
00:43:02,613 --> 00:43:04,591
Will you make it ten-five?
Will you make it ten-five?

795
00:43:04,615 --> 00:43:05,826
Will you make it
ten-five? Ten-five!

796
00:43:05,850 --> 00:43:07,795
10,500, now 11,000.

797
00:43:07,819 --> 00:43:09,310
Ten-five, now 11.
Will you bet 11?

798
00:43:12,223 --> 00:43:14,568
Negatives?!

799
00:43:14,592 --> 00:43:17,004
You mean, you mean,
they're being blackmailed?

800
00:43:17,028 --> 00:43:19,573
Yeah. And from what I heard,
it's been going on for years.

801
00:43:19,597 --> 00:43:21,708
Sherry's just taking
up where Eric left off.

802
00:43:21,732 --> 00:43:24,344
They're after the negatives,
they're not after the ledger.

803
00:43:24,368 --> 00:43:26,360
Huh.

804
00:43:30,875 --> 00:43:31,852
Hello.

805
00:43:31,876 --> 00:43:33,420
Hello. Mr. Matlock?

806
00:43:33,444 --> 00:43:34,855
Sherry?

807
00:43:34,879 --> 00:43:37,024
Mr. Matlock, I'm scared.

808
00:43:37,048 --> 00:43:39,026
They're gonna kill me,
just like they killed Eric.

809
00:43:39,050 --> 00:43:40,227
Where are you?

810
00:43:40,251 --> 00:43:42,229
I'm at a friend's cottage.

811
00:43:42,253 --> 00:43:45,099
I-I thought it would be safer.

812
00:43:45,123 --> 00:43:46,667
Listen, there's something
I haven't told you.

813
00:43:46,691 --> 00:43:48,102
We need to talk.

814
00:43:48,126 --> 00:43:51,038
About how you've been
blackmailing those three men?

815
00:43:51,062 --> 00:43:53,340
How did you know?

816
00:43:53,364 --> 00:43:54,575
You answer my question first.

817
00:43:54,599 --> 00:43:56,076
Now, what have you got on them?

818
00:43:56,100 --> 00:44:00,080
Meet me tomorrow
at the parking lot

819
00:44:00,104 --> 00:44:02,416
at Lake Wheeler, and
I'll tell you everything.

820
00:44:02,440 --> 00:44:05,686
What's wrong with right now?

821
00:44:05,710 --> 00:44:08,055
I hid something that
I need to show you.

822
00:44:08,079 --> 00:44:10,257
The negatives?

823
00:44:10,281 --> 00:44:12,126
You know?

824
00:44:12,150 --> 00:44:14,628
Yeah.

825
00:44:14,652 --> 00:44:17,264
Well, I... I can't get them
till tomorrow morning.

826
00:44:17,288 --> 00:44:20,567
The parking lot, Lake Wheeler...
Can you be there at 9:00?

827
00:44:20,591 --> 00:44:21,568
You bet.

828
00:44:21,592 --> 00:44:23,670
See you then.

829
00:44:23,694 --> 00:44:25,873
Well, Conrad... Huh?

830
00:44:25,897 --> 00:44:29,443
We're gonna see
the sun rise tomorrow.

831
00:44:29,467 --> 00:44:30,467
Okay.

832
00:45:06,971 --> 00:45:08,282
9:00 on the button.

833
00:45:08,306 --> 00:45:09,306
Hmm.

834
00:45:18,916 --> 00:45:20,680
There she is.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
